          "path": "_m/w/9/z/h/casa-real-de-iloilo-wp/casa-real-de-iloilo.jpg",
          "filename": "Casa Real de Iloilo.jpg",
          "caption": "The Casa Real de Iloilo, which was finished in 1873 during the Spanish era and originally used as the governor's mansion, is where the history of the Iloilo Provincial Capitol began. In 1901, the United States established it as the seat of civil administration. Philippine Commission. After suffering damage during World War II, the structure was reconstructed, underwent extensive renovations in the 1960s, and again caught fire in 1998. Behind it, a brand-new, contemporary, six-story capitol was constructed, while the old Casa Real was restored in two years after being designated a historical landmark in 2010.",
          "alt": "The Casa Real de Iloilo, which was finished in 1873 during the Spanish era and originally used as the governor's mansion, is where the history of the Iloilo Provincial Capitol began. In 1901, the United States established it as the seat of civil administration. Philippine Commission. After suffering damage during World War II, the structure was reconstructed, underwent extensive renovations in the 1960s, and again caught fire in 1998. Behind it, a brand-new, contemporary, six-story capitol was constructed, while the old Casa Real was restored in two years after being designated a historical landmark in 2010.",
          "width": 1926,
          "height": 1348,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
